            <ArticleTitle>[The correlation between interleukin-1 receptor antagonist genotype and coronary heart disease in patients with chronic periodontitis].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="PURPOSE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To investigate the correlation between interleukin-1 receptor antagonist (IL-1ra) genotype and chronic periodontitis in patients with coronary heart disease.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Genomic DNA was obtained from buccal swabs in 86 patients with coronary heart disease,of which 45 patients with chronic periodontitis, the other without chronic periodontitis. Genotypes of IL-1RN intron 2 VNTR were analyzed by SSP-PCR method. Then the differences in distribution of each genotype were analyzed with SPSS 13.0 software package.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">A significant over-representation of IL-1 RN intron 2 VNTR allele 2 was found in patients with coronary heart disease and chronic periodontitis group (chi(2)=4.960,P=0.026).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">IL-1RN intron 2 VNTR allele 2 may be a risk indicator for the susceptibility of chronic periodontitis in patients with coronary heart disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
